<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 117 0 R
/T (1NF. All attributes are atomic and repeating groups \(many payments, complaints, mess months and visitors per student\) are moved into separate tables, each with a primary key.)
/E (1NF. All attributes are atomic and repeating groups \(many payments, complaints, mess months and visitors per student\) are moved into separate tables, each with a primary key.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 117 0 R
/T (2NF. No partial dependencies. Room details \(room_no, capacity, status\) depend only on room_id and are stored in Room, not repeated in Student. Block details depend only on block_id and are stored in Hostel_Block.)
/E (2NF. No partial dependencies. Room details \(room_no, capacity, status\) depend only on room_id and are stored in Room, not repeated in Student. Block details depend only on block_id and are stored in Hostel_Block.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 117 0 R
/T (3NF. Transitive dependencies are removed. A student's block and warden are not stored in Student: Student references Room, Room references Hostel_Block, and Hostel_Block references the warden in Staff \(student to room to block to warden\). Warden name and phone therefore appear only once, in Staff.)
/E (3NF. Transitive dependencies are removed. A student's block and warden are not stored in Student: Student references Room, Room references Hostel_Block, and Hostel_Block references the warden in Staff \(student to room to block to warden\). Warden name and phone therefore appear only once, in Staff.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
