1433 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system is built on a normalised MySQL database of eight related tables connected through primary and foreign keys. The application is developed with Node.js \(v24.15.0\), run with npm start, and provides a browser interface with a sidebar for each module where an administrator can insert, view and delete records. Drop-down lists are filled from related tables so that only valid foreign-key values can be chosen. SQL joins, aggregates and subqueries generate reports such as room occupancy, block-wise strength, unpaid fees and open complaints.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 991 0 R
/Prev 1311 0 R
/Next 1312 0 R
>>
endobj
1434 0 obj
<<
/Title (who stays in which room, which rooms are free, who has paid fees, which complaints are pending, which mess plan each student has taken and who visited whom. Doing this manually is error-prone and time-consuming.)
